WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:20.209
"Mrs. Sweet?" Maggie exclaimed. "She'd never steal anything from anybody!"

2
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.218
"Yeah," Cole said. "Mrs. Sweet is great."

3
00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:29.744
Henry nodded. "I know you're new in town," he told Mr. Tate.

4
00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:34.120
"But everyone in Belltown knows how nice Mrs. Sweet is.

5
00:00:34.121 --> 00:00:38.299
The Sweet Shop has been around since our parents were little."

6
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.402
"Exactly," Mr. Tate said with a frown.

7
00:00:41.403 --> 00:00:45.174
"Mrs. Sweet doesn't want any competition from the Dessert Den!"

8
00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:50.210
"What makes you think Mrs. Sweet stole your flavor?" Cole asked.

9
00:00:50.211 --> 00:00:54.335
"That's a good question." Henry turned to Mr. Tate.

10
00:00:54.336 --> 00:00:57.643
"You haven't told us exactly what happened."

11
00:00:57.644 --> 00:01:00.461
"Oh right," Mr. Tate said.

12
00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:05.136
"Like I said, I invented a unique flavor of ice cream for the grand opening.

13
00:01:05.137 --> 00:01:09.972
I haven't told a soul in Belltown about it. It was top secret!"

14
00:01:09.973 --> 00:01:12.868
"Then what happened?" Maggie asked.

15
00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:16.924
"Did someone break in here and steal the ice cream out of your freezer?"

16
00:01:16.925 --> 00:01:20.241
"No, nothing like that," Mr. Tate said.

17
00:01:20.242 --> 00:01:24.250
"In fact, my ice-cream order isn't scheduled to arrive until this afternoon.

18
00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:29.874
But just this morning, I saw my flavor listed on the chalkboard outside the Sweet Shop!"

19
00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:36.247
The Lemonade Detectives exchanged looks. "Really? That's weird," Cole said.

20
00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:39.749
"It doesn't prove anything, though," Maggie said.

21
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.081
"Mrs. Sweet makes up new flavors all the time.

22
00:01:43.082 --> 00:01:46.712
Maybe she came up with the same idea on her own."

23
00:01:46.713 --> 00:01:48.731
Mr. Tate shook his head.

24
00:01:48.732 --> 00:01:55.167
"I doubt it. How likely is it that she just happened to make up a flavor like bubble gum banana swirl?"

25
00:01:55.168 --> 00:01:58.788
"Bubble gum banana swirl?" Henry echoed.

26
00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:03.257
He and Cole had seen that flavor on the Sweet Shop sign themselves.

27
00:02:03.258 --> 00:02:06.086
It was one of today's special flavors!

28
00:02:06.087 --> 00:02:09.546
"Right. That's my flavor. See?"

29
00:02:09.547 --> 00:02:14.037
Mr. Tate strode over to the menu sign and pulled back the sheet.

30
00:02:14.038 --> 00:02:21.372
The sign said Dessert Den Grand Opening Exclusive: Bubble gum Banana Swirl Ice Cream!

31
00:02:21.373 --> 00:02:26.297
"How do you think Mrs. Sweet heard about your flavor?" Henry asked.

32
00:02:26.298 --> 00:02:30.829
Mr. Tate shrugged. "I assume someone at the factory told her."

33
00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.607
"What factory?" Cole asked.

34
00:02:33.608 --> 00:02:37.997
"The place where I'm having all my ice cream made," Mr. Tate explained.

35
00:02:37.998 --> 00:02:42.430
"I tell the owners what flavors I want, and they make it for me."

36
00:02:42.431 --> 00:02:46.180
"Mrs. Sweet doesn't use a factory," Maggie said.

37
00:02:46.181 --> 00:02:49.978
"She makes all her own flavors in the back of her shop."

38
00:02:49.979 --> 00:02:53.387
"She does?" Mr. Tate looked surprised.

39
00:02:53.388 --> 00:02:58.699
"Yes," Henry said. "So she couldn't have heard about it from the factory."

40
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.582
Mr. Tate tugged on the sheet to cover his sign again.

41
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:07.391
"Okay, I just thought of another way it could have happened," he said.

42
00:03:07.392 --> 00:03:09.983
"I've been keeping my menu covered up.

43
00:03:09.984 --> 00:03:14.393
But a few days ago the painter forgot to cover it before leaving for the night.

44
00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:17.705
Somebody could have looked in the window and seen it then."

45
00:03:17.706 --> 00:03:24.383
"You mean you think Mrs. Sweet sneaked over here at night and peeked in at your flavors?" Cole said.

46
00:03:24.384 --> 00:03:27.271
"That doesn't sound like something she would do."

47
00:03:27.272 --> 00:03:29.065
Henry agreed with that.

48
00:03:29.066 --> 00:03:32.850
But as he looked around the Dessert Den, he had a moment of doubt.

49
00:03:32.851 --> 00:03:35.896
Mr. Tate's new shop really looked great.

50
00:03:35.897 --> 00:03:43.257
It had a brand-new ice-cream counter, the cool hand-painted sign, and a shiny silver soda fountain.

51
00:03:43.258 --> 00:03:46.943
It was a lot fancier than the old-fashioned Sweet Shop.

52
00:03:46.944 --> 00:03:50.414
Could Mrs. Sweet really be worried about the competition?

53
00:03:50.415 --> 00:03:54.188
Maybe even worried enough to sabotage the Dessert Den?

54
00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:56.672
"No," Henry said out loud.

55
00:03:56.673 --> 00:04:01.034
"I can't believe Mrs. Sweet would steal your flavor idea.

56
00:04:01.035 --> 00:04:04.112
There must be another explanation."

57
00:04:04.113 --> 00:04:06.772
"Oh yeah?" Mr. Tate frowned.

58
00:04:06.773 --> 00:04:09.608
"I thought you kids were supposed to be detectives.

59
00:04:09.609 --> 00:04:14.279
The evidence is right there on my menu—and on her flavor board!"

60
00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:18.413
"Mrs. Sweet has the same flavor as you," Maggie said.

61
00:04:18.414 --> 00:04:21.293
"But that doesn't mean she's a thief."

62
00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:25.200
Henry nodded. "Maggie is right," he said.

63
00:04:25.201 --> 00:04:28.160
"It's just circumstantial evidence."

64
00:04:28.161 --> 00:04:31.984
"What kind of evidence?" Cole looked confused.

65
00:04:31.985 --> 00:04:34.868
"Circumstantial," Henry said.

66
00:04:34.869 --> 00:04:39.928
"It's evidence that implies something, but doesn't actually prove it."

67
00:04:39.929 --> 00:04:45.028
"Okay," Mr. Tate said. "So how do you explain what happened then?"

68
00:04:45.029 --> 00:04:50.337
"I'm not sure yet," Henry said. "We need to investigate and figure it out.

69
00:04:50.338 --> 00:04:55.668
We'll get back to you later."

70
00:04:55.669 --> 00:05:00.774
When the Lemonade Detectives got outside, they stopped by their bikes to talk.

71
00:05:00.775 --> 00:05:06.036
"You don't really think Mrs. Sweet is a thief, do you?" Maggie asked Henry.

72
00:05:06.037 --> 00:05:08.867
"Of course not," Henry said.

73
00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:13.993
"But it's really odd that they both ended up with that same flavor."

74
00:05:13.994 --> 00:05:21.854
Cole nodded. "Yeah. And it's not a common flavor like mint chocolate chip or fudge ripple," he said.

75
00:05:21.855 --> 00:05:28.658
"There's no way Mrs. Sweet and Mr. Tate both invented bubble gum banana swirl in the same week!"

76
00:05:28.659 --> 00:05:33.999
"I agree," said Henry. "We need to start our investigation."

77
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.991
"How do we do that?" Maggie asked.

78
00:05:36.992 --> 00:05:42.645
Henry bit his lip, thinking. "I guess we need to go question Mrs. Sweet.

79
00:05:42.646 --> 00:05:48.435
Even if it's just to rule her out as a suspect."
